# =============================================================
# If you have both managed_scan and sample_ros2_app in the same pod/container, and you use ros2 lifecycle set managed_scan_node shutdown, it will change the lifecycle state of the managed_scan node to "finalized".
# However, the process (and thus the container) is still running. The node is in a state where it cannot be restarted without restarting the entire process that created it.
Then If i config two apps in OSS/oss_multisw_framework/docker/kubernetes_envrironment/ros2/ros2-sample-check.yaml : managed_scan and sample_ros2_app. And If i terminate managed_scan only via ros2 lifecycle set .... shutdown. There's no way start managed_scan app only?

GitHub Copilot
Correct—if both managed_scan and sample_ros2_app are started by a single launch file or single process (as in your current YAML), and you use ros2 lifecycle set managed_scan_node shutdown, only the lifecycle state of the node changes. The process (and thus the container) is still running, but the node is in the "finalized" state and cannot be restarted without restarting the process.

In this setup, you cannot restart only the managed_scan node from "finalized" state without restarting the whole container (and thus both apps).

Why?
The ROS 2 lifecycle only manages the node's internal state, not the process itself.
Once a node is in "finalized", it cannot be brought back to "unconfigured" or "active" without restarting the process that created it.
Since both nodes are in the same process/container, you cannot restart just one node's process.
How to Enable Independent Restart
If you want to be able to restart managed_scan independently:

Run each app in a separate container (recommended for Kubernetes best practices).
Each container should have its own command/launch file for its node.
Then, you can restart the pod/container for just managed_scan without affecting sample_ros2_app.
Example:

One pod/container for managed_scan
One pod/container for sample_ros2_app
Summary:
With your current YAML (both apps in one container), you cannot restart only managed_scan after shutdown.
To enable independent restart, run each app in its own container. This is the standard Kubernetes approach for microservices and ROS 2 multi-node deployments.
